
### TEST 1: Successful registration
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test Student",
    "email": "student1@example.com",
    "password": "Student123"
}

###

### TEST 2: Missing required fields
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test Student"
}

###

### TEST 3: Invalid email
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test Student",
    "email": "invalid-email",
    "password": "Student123"
}

###

### TEST 4: Password shorter than 8 characters
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test Student",
    "email": "student2@example.com",
    "password": "12345"
}

###

### TEST 5: Duplicate email
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Another Student",
    "email": "student1@example.com",
    "password": "Another123"
}

### TEST 6: Get all users
GET http://localhost:5000/api/users

###

### TEST 7: Create a dedicated CRUD test user
POST http://localhost:5000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "CRUD Test Student",
    "email": "crud.student.step6@example.com",
    "password": "CrudTest123"
}

###

### TEST 8: Get one user by ID
GET http://localhost:5000/api/users/1

###

### TEST 9: Get user with invalid ID
GET http://localhost:5000/api/users/abc

###

### TEST 10: Get user that does not exist
GET http://localhost:5000/api/users/999999

###

### TEST 11: Update user
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Updated CRUD Student",
    "email": "crud.student.updated.step6@example.com"
}

###

### TEST 12: Update with invalid email
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Updated CRUD Student",
    "email": "invalid-email"
}

